cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "COUNTEREXAMPLE: A Public Engineering Failure Museum"
message: "If this artifact supports your work, cite the archived software release."
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-10
authors:
  - family-names: Patel
    given-names: Aaryan
repository-code: "https://github.com/asp53826/counterexample"
url: "https://asp53826.github.io/counterexample/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A constrained, reproducible archive of twelve real failure regimes drawn from
  distributed systems, autonomy, quantitative engineering, ML compilers,
  approximate search, and synthetic aperture radar. Each capsule binds a
  trigger, invariant, source location, verification command, limitation, and
  self-contained receipt to an exact public commit.
keywords:
  - reproducibility
  - distributed systems
  - failure analysis
  - counterexample
  - software verification
